.Dd November 4, 2026
.Dt EIOIC 4 loongarch64
.Os
.\" .Nm loongarch64/eioic
.Sh NAME
.Nm eioic
.Nd LoongArch extended I/O interrupt controller
.Sh SYNOPSIS
This driver is a standard part of the LoongArch kernel.
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
driver provides support for the extended I/O interrupt controller
(EIOINTC) used by Loongson systems.
It manages external interrupt vectors and dispatches them through
.Xr cpuic 4 .
The
.Xr pch_pic 4
controller uses these vectors to deliver platform device interrupts.
.Pp
On ACPI systems the controller is instantiated by the platform nexus.
When ACPI is absent, it can attach to flattened device tree nodes with
either of the following compatible strings:
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
.Qq loongson,eiointc
.It
.Qq loongson,ls2k2000-eiointc
.El
.Pp
External interrupts can be assigned to a CPU with
.Xr cpuset 1 .
The driver translates logical CPU numbers to hardware node and core
routing fields.
Unbound vectors remain on the boot CPU.
.Pp
No driver-specific kernel configuration directive is required.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr cpuset 1 ,
.Xr acpi 4 ,
.Xr cpuic 4 ,
.Xr fdt 4 ,
.Xr pch_pic 4
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
driver was added in the LoongArch port of
.Fx 16.0 .
